"# Continuity packet
You are continuing work on this project. This packet is your context; there is no earlier conversation to read.

## Charter and goal
Project: acme-web
Goal: Ship authentication
Lane: Login

## Active constraints (always follow)
- [C-1] Never commit secrets

## Accepted project decisions
- [D-1] superseded by D-2; no longer holds: Use SQLite
- [D-2] Use Postgres (db.engine = postgres) [unverified]. Why: need concurrency

## This lane's branch decisions
- [D-3] Validate input with zod [unverified]. Why: one schema per route

## Your current task
- [T-1] Add login endpoint (claimed until 2026-09-22T11:00:00.000Z)
- Acceptance: POST /api/login returns a session cookie

## Computed state (from git and test runs, not self-reported)
Branch: feat-api
HEAD: a1b2c3d
Last green commit: a1b2c3d

## Failed or abandoned attempts in this area (do not repeat)
- [A-1] src/api/auth.ts: tried JWT in localStorage; failed because XSS exposure

## Current hypothesis
- [H-1] Cookie is dropped by the proxy
- For: no Set-Cookie at client
- Ruled out: server never sets it
- Next experiment: curl the proxy directly

## Other active lanes
- Lane Billing on feat-billing; files: src/billing/stripe.ts

## Index of all records (fetch details with get_record)
- A-1 attempt: src/api/auth.ts: JWT in localStorage
- C-1 constraint: Never commit secrets
- D-1 decision: Use SQLite (superseded by D-2)
- D-2 decision: Use Postgres
- D-3 decision: Validate input with zod
- H-1 hypothesis: Cookie is dropped by the proxy
- T-1 task: Add login endpoint

## Last turns in this lane (verbatim; tool output stubbed)
- user: Why is the cookie missing?
- tool: [command_execution curl -i localhost:3000/api/login exit 0; ref item-9]

## How to use shared memory
Shared project memory is on the t3-code MCP server. Other agents and future sessions rely on it, so keep it current:
- Cite record IDs in brackets, such as [D-12], whenever you rely on a record.
- Record each decision with propose_decision, each failed or abandoned approach with record_attempt, and your working theory with update_hypothesis, as you go rather than at the end.
- Call declare_intent before editing an area other lanes may touch, and claim_task before starting a task.
- Call request_task_done only after committing and running the tests; it checks the test result itself.
- Anything not shown here is available through search_memory, get_record, expand and whats_new.

# End of packet"
